  "body": "### Summary\nAs the maintainer, I want the smiley and GIF pickers to share one image loader per picker (or per app), so that showing a grid of thumbnails does not create a fetcher, a transport and URL sessions for each cell, with no connection reuse to the same host.\n\n### Evidence (`dev-swift` @ 90b23273, read from the code, not measured)\n- `App/SwiftHFR/Smileys/SmileyThumbnailView.swift:49-51`: `makeCoordinator()` returns `Coordinator(loader: source == .gif ? .gif() : SmileyImageLoader())`. Each coordinator, so each thumbnail view identity, builds its own `SmileyImageLoader`. That loader owns a `ReaderImageFetcher()` with its default `AnonymousTransport`, and its URL sessions (`URLSessionTransport`: a base session plus the no-follow session).\n- The comment at `:58` (\"Built once per cell: a loader per update would leak an HTTP session each time\") avoids one build per update, not one per cell.\n- Callers:\n  - smiley picker grid and preview: `SmileyPickerView.swift:280,298`;\n  - GIF picker grid and preview: `GifPickerView.swift:86,149,151`.\n- The decoded-image cache is already shared (`SmileyImageLoader`'s static `NSCache`), so only the transports are duplicated.\n\n### Scope\n- Build one loader per source (forum smileys, GIF), shared by the cells: a static per source, or one owned by the picker and passed down.\n- Keep the host rules as they are: `allowsThirdParty: false` for smileys, `.gif()` (Giphy CDN only) for GIFs.\n- Same pattern as #1249, where the image panel's thumbnail loader was moved to one per panel.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- Showing N thumbnails builds at most one `ReaderImageFetcher` per source, checked by a test through a counting seam or by construction.\n- The loader's host filter stays the same for each source (a test, as in #1249's `thePanelsLoaderFiltersOnTheRehostHost`).\n\n### Origin\nA finding of the adversarial review of #1255 (#1249, a #775 review follow-up), outside that PR's scope. `m4-review: quality` is not set on purpose: this was not opened by the #775 review itself.",
